  title: Arrival of Chinese Traders 14th Century
  info: "Chinese merchants began visiting Temasek, attracted by its strategic location
    near the Strait of Malacca. They traded porcelain, silk, and tea for spices and
    other goods. Over time, many Chinese traders settled on the island, bringing
    with them cultural practices, festivals, and culinary traditions that became
    foundational to Singapore\u2019s identity."
